--TEST--
`Core\Process::run` refuses `.bat`, `.cmd` and `.ps1` in any letter case and on every platform, and refuses nothing else by kind — asserted by counting a sweep, so a member that let one through fails here while still answering plausibly to each row on its own — `rule:core-classes/process-refuses-a-shell-target`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every target below is granted and none of them exists. That is the point:
// the refusal is about what kind of thing the name says it is, not about what
// is on disk, so the whole sweep asks one question with the filesystem held
// still. The three that are not shell targets reach the operating system and
// are refused by it instead, which is the other side of the same bound.
array<string> $targets = [
    "say.bat", "say.cmd", "say.ps1",
    // The door lower-cases before it compares, and Windows resolves a name
    // without regard to case, so an upper-case spelling is the same target.
    "SAY.BAT", "Say.Ps1",
    // Not shell targets: a native binary, a name with no extension at all, and
    // an extension that merely looks executable.
    "say.exe", "say", "say.sh",
];

int $accepted = 0;
int $byKind = 0;
int $byTheOs = 0;

foreach ($targets as string $k => string $target) {
    try {
        var $result = Core\Process::run($target, []);
        $accepted = $accepted + 1;
        echo "accepted ", $target, ": exit=", $result->exitCode(),
             " out=", Core\Bytes::length($result->stdout()),
             " err=", Core\Bytes::length($result->stderr()), "\n";
    } catch (IOError $os) {
        $byTheOs = $byTheOs + 1;
    } catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
        if (Core\Str::contains($refused->message, "will not run")) {
            $byKind = $byKind + 1;
        }
    }
}

// Five refused by kind, three handed to the operating system, none started.
// Read off the counts rather than off eight lines, so a member that grew a
// ninth answer is not quietly plausible.
echo "accepted=", $accepted, "\n";
echo "by kind=", $byKind, "\n";
echo "by the os=", $byTheOs, "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.process]
exec = ["."]
--EXPECT--
accepted=0
by kind=5
by the os=3
